 y Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Deve
 lopment\nSeptember Safety Classes\nAugust 18\, 2026\nDear Employer\,\nWork
 place safety and labor law requirements can seem complex - join the Maine 
 Department of Labor for no-cost upcoming trainings! Please forward to your
  Safety Coordinators/Managers.\nUpcoming classes:\nLife Safety Code 101- S
 eptember 1\, 2026 I 8:30 a.m.  4:30 p.m.\nSafetyWorks! Training Institute\
 , Department of Labor\, 45 Commerce Drive\, Augusta\nThis one-day class wi
 ll provide a working overview of National Fire Protection Association (NFP
 A) Standard 101 "Life Safety Code" for fire and life safety in the buildin
 g environment. Topics covered will include classification of occupancy typ
 es\, adequate means of egress\, occupant load factors\, and occupancy spec
 ific hazards to fire and life safety. The Life Safety Code is adopted in t
 he State of Maine as the state code for fire and life safety in buildings.
 \nLifting & Rigging Safety  September 3\, 2026 I 8:30 a.m.  12:30 p.m.\nSa
 fetyWorks! Training Institute\, Department of Labor\, 45 Commerce Drive\, 
 Augusta\nLift planning is essential to safe-lifting practices. This progra
 m will explore lifting and rigging equipment\, inspections\, signaling\, a
 nd planning for safe lifts.\nWage & Hour Compliance September 9\, 2026 I 9
 :00 a.m.  12:00 p.m.\nUniversity of New England\, 11 Hills Beach Road\, Ma
 rcil Hall\, Room 124\, Biddeford\nThis course is designed for human resour
 ce or benefits professionals\, accountants\, business owners\, managers\, 
 or payroll supervisors. Labor laws can be complex. This seminar covers wag
 e and hour laws\, incl\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.sht
 ml?id=13358835
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13358835
