SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Competitive Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP)
  Rule Changes Effective August 2\, 2026
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Competitive 
 Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP) Rule Changes Effective August 2\, 2026\n
 Services\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment Insurance\nDisability Services\nWo
 rkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nCompe
 titive Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP) Rule Changes Effective August 2\,
  2026\nAugust 5\, 2026\nThe Maine Department of Labor has updated the Comp
 etitive Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP) rules to implement recent statut
 ory changes\, expand participant supports\, improve program flexibility\, 
 and clarify program requirements. The revised rules took effect on August 
 2\, 2026.\nSome of the most significant changes include:\nExpanded monthly
  stipend eligibility.\nMore students may now qualify for a monthly CSSP st
 ipend because income eligibility limits have increased.\nPartial stipends 
 for part-time students.\nEligible part-time students may now receive a pro
 rated monthly stipend based on their enrollment status and income.\nExpand
 ed support services.\nEligible participants may qualify for increased assi
 stance with transportation\, vehicle repairs\, and other necessary needs u
 nder higher support service funding limits.\nExpanded educational opportun
 ities.\nEligibility has also been expanded for applicants with pre-existin
 g preparatory associate degree programs.\nImproved program clarity and acc
 essibility.\nThe revised rules simplify eligibility requirements\, clarify
  appeal rights\, improve communication preferences\, and increase transpar
 ency regarding the High-Wage\, In-Demand Occupations list.\nNew CSSP Cohor
 t funding opportunities.\nTraining providers and their partners will be in
 vited to apply for CSSP Cohort funding. The Maine Department of Labor will
  host a lis\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13357
 590
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13357590
